The old dropdown had a **Delete comment** item that called `handleDeleteClick(item)`. The PR removes that item and `handleDeleteClick`. Nothing calls `setCommentToDelete(comment)` any more, so `commentToDelete` can never be non-null.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="326-346"}

The `useDeleteComment` hook, `confirmDelete` and the whole `AlertDialog` are still in place, but they're dead code:

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="149-157"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Moderators can no longer delete a comment from this screen, which is a core moderation action. The PR description doesn't mention removing it. If it was intentional, delete the dialog and mutation too. If it wasn't, restore the menu item.


To restore it, add the item back to the dropdown:

::suggestion{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="344-345"}
                                                    {item.status !== 'deleted' && (
                                                        <DropdownMenuItem
                                                            className="text-destructive focus:text-destructive"
                                                            onClick={() => setCommentToDelete(item)}
                                                        >
                                                            <LucideIcon.Trash2 className="mr-2 size-4" />
                                                            Delete comment
                                                        </DropdownMenuItem>
                                                    )}
                                                </DropdownMenuContent>

`useInfiniteVirtualScroll` uses `virtualItem.key` as the row key, and TanStack Virtual defaults that to the **index** (no `getItemKey` is passed). `CommentContent` has no key of its own, and its measuring effect runs only once (`[]` deps):

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="87-104"}

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="261-261"}

When the items at an index change, React reuses the component instance at that index. That happens when you apply a filter (now one click away on the author or post name), remove a filter, or delete or refetch comments. The new comment then inherits the old one's `isExpanded`, and `isClamped` is never recomputed. A long comment can show no "Show more" button and stay stuck at two lines, or a short comment can show a useless button.

Keying the component by comment id fixes both problems:

::suggestion{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="261-261"}
                                        <CommentContent key={item.id} item={item} />

It's also worth re-running `checkIfClamped` when `item.html` changes, or using a `ResizeObserver`.

`formatNumber` in shade is typed `(value: number): string`, but these calls pass `item.count?.replies` (`number | undefined`). `apps/posts/tsconfig.json` has `strict: true`, and the package's build script is `tsc && vite build`, so this should fail with TS2345. At runtime it happens to work (`isNaN(undefined)` returns `'0'`), but only by accident.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="281-309"}

::suggestion{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="281-281"}
                                                                <span>{formatNumber(item.count?.replies ?? 0)}</span>

Make the same change for `likes` (line 295) and `reports` (line 309).

`checkIfClamped` also runs on `resize`. When the comment is expanded, `line-clamp-2` is removed, so `scrollHeight === clientHeight` and `isClamped` becomes `false`. The "Show less" button then disappears, and the comment stays expanded with no way to collapse it until you reload.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="93-116"}

Skip the measurement while expanded, or always render the button when `isExpanded` is true:

::suggestion{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="114-116"}
                {(isClamped || isExpanded) && (
                    <ExpandButton expanded={isExpanded} onClick={() => setIsExpanded(!isExpanded)} />
                )}

Template expressions like `${item.status === 'hidden' && 'text-muted-foreground'}` put the string `"false"` into `className` for every published comment. On the author button, `text-primary` and `text-muted-foreground` can also both apply. Which colour wins then depends on stylesheet order, not on the order in the class string, so hidden authors may not look muted.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="194-200"}

Use `cn()` from `@tryghost/shade`, which is clsx plus tailwind-merge, so falsy values are dropped and conflicting utilities are resolved:

::suggestion{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="194-194"}
                                                        className={cn('flex h-auto items-center gap-1.5 truncate p-0 font-semibold text-primary hover:opacity-70', item.status === 'hidden' && 'text-muted-foreground')}

The same pattern is at lines 112 and 200, and `${!item.count?.replies && ...}` at 279/293.

The avatar always shows the fallback icon, even though `member.avatar_image` is already in the API response and in the `Comment` type. The block that would render the real image is commented out instead of being finished or removed.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="200-207"}

Either add `AvatarImage` with `src={item.member.avatar_image}`, or delete the comment block.
